-- The adjugate's informal proof explicitly opens form (its defining pairing),
-- adj at its characterisation, and Linear at the proof of form-linearity.
-- Ext is the recursive representation of its vector arguments; Mat/Vec
-- decode the column matrix at module applications. No map body is allowed.
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.L: isSet
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.M: Mat
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.form:
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.form-linear: Ext form Linear isSet
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.adj:
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.characterise: Ext adj
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.unique: Ext
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.adj-add: Ext form
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.adj-scale: Ext form
ExteriorAdjugate.Over.At.adj-map: Vec Mat Ext form isSet
